TASK-197 runtime harness: dev mode's "under construction" colours compared
(the sidebar's hazard border and the dev toolbar's stripes), five palette
options in light and dark, at 2x. The options live only here; the product has
DevModePalette.standard plus a DEBUG-only DevModePalette.debugOverride.
Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task197-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # Retina on a 1x monitor: the TASK-110 virtual display (docs/task-110/vdisplay.m),
    #   ./vdisplay &  (a 1600x1000 pt @2x screen until killed); the harness
    #   moves the window (1000x620) onto the first 2x screen.
    # $SITE/app.html, api.html, split.html: a <title>, an <h1>, a line of
    # text, <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">.
    python3 -m http.server 8897 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory "$SITE" &
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify197 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8897 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # a watcher runs `screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber> $OUT/<name>.png`
    # for each "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>" line of $OUT/verify.log; the
    # harness waits for each PNG. Wait for "done" (about 50 s), then kill that
    # pid, the server and vdisplay.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task197-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    rm -r -- ~/Library/Application\ Support/DetourVerify197

Rows (top to bottom): a split (Split Local on localhost | a data: page),
Remote Docs (data:, a normal row), API Server (127.0.0.1, unselected dev
row), Dev App (localhost, selected, its toolbar over the page). Each option
sets debugOverride, switches NSApp.appearance, then calls updateColors() on
every HazardBorderView (and sets its shape layers' lineWidth, for E) and
needsDisplay on every DevToolbarView, twice, 1 s apart. Each SHOOT logs a
GEOM line (window, rows, toolbar and selected border rects in window points)
that the contact-sheet script crops by: pixel = (x * s, (H - maxY) * s).

Options (sRGB; dash colour unchanged throughout: white 0.1 light, 0.05 dark):
  A  current: systemYellow (#FFCC00 light, #FFD600 dark); stripes black 3% / white 3.5%
  B  brand orange #FF7600 both; stripes as A
  C  lighter orange #FF9500 light (systemOrange), #FF9F0A dark; stripes as A
  D  B's border; stripes #FF7600 at 10% light, 8% dark
  E  B's colours on a 2 pt line (1.5 pt otherwise), dashes 4/4

Results (2026-10-24, macOS 26.7, window 1000x620 on the 2x virtual display,
captures 2000x1240 px; all ten read, labels matching the log). Sampled from
